WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Yuko Yoshida (15 years old)

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:04.000
One day, a 15-year-old girl named Yuko suddenly awoke

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
as a Demon Girl by sprouting a tail and horns.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:12.000
A RECAP OF THE EVENTS
UNTIL NOW

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.660
In fact, her family are descendants of the Dark Clan

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.000
that has existed since ancient times.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.290
Thou hast inherited the blood of the dark ones.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:20.580
Title: Shadow Mistress Yuko

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.450
I dub thee Shadow Mistress Yuko!

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.620
Thou must vanquish a Magical Girl who lives in this town,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.450
and restore our clan to its former glory!

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.580
Charged with the duty of undoing the seal upon her
family by defeating a Magical Girl, she begins her quest.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.000
In the middle of her adventure, Shadow Mistress Yuko
was overwhelmed by fierce hunger and exhaustion.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.950
It was then that a helping hand was offered to her.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:39.290
Magical Girl
Momo Chiyoda

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.200
You looked like you were hungry.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.290
However, that hand belong to none
other than her mortal enemy: a Magical Girl!

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.750
DON'T THINK THIS MEANS YOU'VE WON!!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.290
A Reliable Informant
Anri

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.290
If you need a job, just say the word!

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.540
Sis! Thank you!

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.540
A Precious Sister
Waiting in the Homeland - Ryoko

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:50.540
The Eternal Queen of Darkness
Shamiko's Mighty Ancestor
Empress Lilith

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.870
Are you shaking in your boots, Magical Girl?

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.540
This is the true extent of my power!

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.950
Just a Dog Passing By

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.410
Daring tactics.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.370
You can't fool me, you assassin!

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.450
Deadly struggles.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.080
Let's obliterate them into nothing.
And then just forget about everything!

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.950
Or some scenes kind of like that.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.620
Ask me anything you wish!

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.000
Fancy action scenes complete with
slow motion and dramatic camera work

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.120
that spins around while it happens.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.870
Don't give up, Shamiko!
Your glorious battle has only just begun!

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.950
This whole recap is totally wrong!

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.330
Well, I wanted to record all of your feats
thus far into my memory.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.330
Did you not enjoy it?

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.700
It was a complete misrepresentation!

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.540
For starters, I have no idea
where that even took place in!

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.410
And I definitely never wore a weird cape like that!
Tama City is just an ordinary residential development!

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.410
If a giant mushroom like this grew in the middle
of the city it would be a huge problem!

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.330
And there were a whole bunch of parts in the second half
that I don't even remember happening!

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.750
Yeah, but didn't it look super cool?

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.910
It was cool, but...

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.700
GOLD

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.830
...the color of the Ancestue
was all wrong for some reason!

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.700
Well, the most important thing
definitely needs some bling.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.700
That is so out of date!

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.330
It's okay, Shamiko.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.080
This is all just a dream that I made.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.910
Just a dream... just a dream...

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.580
Just a dream...

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.950
It WAS a dream!

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.540
The Demon Girl Next Door

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.500
Taiyou mabushisugite

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.330
(Chikachika me o kosutta)

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.250
Omowazu tobidashita yo

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.790
(Dokidoki no hajimiari sa)

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:27.580
Yurayura yureru maegami hidarite de osaetara

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.160
Itsumo no keshiki ga kirameku yo

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.370
(Three, two, one)

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:38.410
Ima sugu tsutaetai futari no himitsu

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.910
Watashitachi nara dekiru yo

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.910
(Itsumo tonari ni ite)

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.910
Kitto

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.580
(Shijiteru kara)

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:53.540
Machikado de mitsuketa daiji na takaramono

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.330
Tatoe kimi ga tooku hanaretemo kanarazu oikakeru yo

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:05.410
Zutto kagayaiteru mirai wa koko ni aru

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.660
Otanoshimi wa kore kara

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.000
The Pink Method!!
The Wheel of Fate is a Round Tire!!

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.750
Hey, Shamiko. It was a dream,
but it wasn't just any old dream.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.870
I worked all night to make that wonderful dream
and you just outright rejected it!

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.750
I appreciate the thought.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.080
But you took it way too far!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.660
At least I know that my Ancestor
talking to me isn't a dream.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.540
Good morning, Yuko.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.540
Mornin' Sis!

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.290
I'm headed to school!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.450
I'm Yuko Yoshida, 15 years old.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.870
I recently became a novice Demon Girl
and set out on a new journey in life.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:03.000
The record of my struggles you saw that my Ancestor
made was totally blown out of proportion, but...

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.620
"Then what was it really like?"

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.450
"How much of it was actually true?"

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.580
It's hard to answer those so please don't ask.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.000
I WILL say that I'm doing my best in my own unique way.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.790
I think the day I finally make Momo give up
and say "Uncle!" is really close at hand!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.200
Heh
Heh
Heh

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.790
Heh. Heh. Heh.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:14.790
G'morning.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.580
Magical Girl! Why are you here?!
Are you over your cold already?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.910
Not yet, I just left home to do some grocery shopping.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.910
Extra Whole Milk
CHICKEN TENDER
SANDWICH

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.910
Your diet seems way too simple.
I think you should really add-in some vegetables.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.660
I'm not really interested in making more complex meals.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.290
Are you worried about me?

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.450
N-not at all!

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.750
I'm just concerned I won't be able
to steal as much magic from you!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.540
Oh, I have an idea! I've been learning
how to cook from my mom lately.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.370
I'll use you as my guinea pig.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.290
Heh, heh, heh.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:37.910
Already Gone

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:38.660
Already Gone

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:39.410
Already Gone

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.500
Wait, damn you! Are you running away?!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.540
No.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.830
I'm supposed to be taking a sick day from school
so I shouldn't loiter outside.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.290
But speaking of magic...

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.330
Hm? What's up?

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.790
Based on how much I lost, there should be other
changes aside from Ms. Lilith getting more annoying.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:52.790
Huh?

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.910
Hello, you've reached the Yoshida residence.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.410
Excuse me, I'm an officer from the Tama City Police.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.370
May I speak with Ms. Seiko Yoshida?

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.910
Yes, that's me.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.660
I'm home!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.870
Did something happen, mom?

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.120
It all came back.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.750
My purse that fell into the gutter
and the $1,080 that was inside of it!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.540
$1,000?!

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.660
Sorry, my entire concept of the universe
was just turned upside down for second.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:24.700
I think this is proof that the "$400 a Month" curse
has finally been lifted.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.700
Huh?

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.040
Coming in contact with a Magical Girl,
one of the priests of the Light Clan...

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:32.500
Yuko, you have made a major accomplishment!

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.080
Tonight, we shall perform the "ritual"
long passed down in our family!

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.700
ZAP

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.870
Mom, you don't mean we're going to do THAT?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:42.830
I do!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.040
The Yoshida family motto!

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.830
"Whenever fortune smiles upon us, that means
it is definitely our fate to sit around the hot plate!"

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.790
The power just went out for a second, that was scary...

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.620
So without further ado, I went ahead
and purchased groceries for the foreseeable future.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.830
Let's separate and sort them out.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:56.290
Right!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.790
Cabbage, bonito flakes, flour...

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.000
These are ingredients for the okonomiyaki
we're having tonight!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.910
There's wieners and yakisoba noodles, too!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.830
The rest of it is stock for other meals.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.660
Sliced pork, green onions, yellow onions,

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.540
bean sprouts, eggs, bean sprouts, carrots, bean sprouts,

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.330
pudding, bean sprouts, chicken, chicken, chicken,

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.160
bean sprouts, cucumbers and more bean sprouts.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.200
Bean Sprouts

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:19.790
I'm sorry. I just couldn't bring myself
to actually buy the things that are truly luxurious.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:24.330
Although Yuko did remove part of the seal
placed on our family, we still need to take it easy for now.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.750
Because the truth is that there are still various powers
and fortunes of ours that are being held back.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.950
If we give in to our urges now, we'll only be sad
when fate adjusts to make us pay for it all later.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.040
Gulp.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.330
Fate adjusts to make us pay...

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.500
Snap

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.040
Oh no, not our one and only pancake turner!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.500
Can we still make the okonomiyaki?!

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.290
I'll make do with a wooden spatula!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.160
Hey Seiko.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:42.620
Huh?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.790
Do you mind if I butt in?

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:48.750
My husband has told me quite a lot about you,
but this is the first time we've spoken directly.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.750
N-nice to meet you! I'm Yuko's little sister, Ryoko!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.250
Yes, I know of you both.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.790
Although not in much detail.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.200
I'm shocked we can hear your voice so clearly now.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.080
Indeed! This means an end to all those days
I suffered as a doorstop and meat pounder!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:07.950
Monthly Prattle Magazine
Survival Wits Magazine

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.620
Special:
Meals Made Just From Weeds

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.910
Although, because you would always
leave me lying around like some kind of dumbbell

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.950
I was able to learn quite a lot about the modern era.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.330
My apologies.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.660
Heh, heh, heh, heh, heh...

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.830
Since I've now made a mini-revival, I think it's about time
I flex my muscle as the family patriarch.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.160
There's a lot I want to ask you, for starters-

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:16.580
Super Buzz - Mikan Flavor

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.790
Oh, dear Ancestor?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.450
We're about to have a little celebration right now
so could you hold that off until later?

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.250
What is this?

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.830
Just a can of fizzy goodness.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:28.160
Super Buzz - Mikan Flavor

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.290
I've never seen this before,
is it another sweet carbonated beverage?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.200
I have to admit it's pretty tasty, but...

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:28.160
Hiccup!

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.160
Ancestor!

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.580
Wha... What the heck is happening?!

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.450
The world is spinning like a top! Was that poison?!

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.120
But it's really addictive...

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.250
It's a canned highball.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.290
Ancestor, what did you want to talk to us about?

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.160
Hm? Hiccup...

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.910
Oh, Ancestor?

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:49.370
SHINSHUU BRAND
DEMON EXTERMINATOR

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:43.450
Squeak!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:46.580
I prepared you a nice sake bath.
It's the most luxurious thing you can imagine!

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.580
Squeak! Squeak! Squeak!

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.620
Faint...

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:49.370
ANCESTOR!

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.250
It's party time right now, so please refrain from
bringing up any complicated topics of discussion.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.910
I hope we'll be able to get along well as housemates.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.250
Okay, great grandmother-in-law?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.910
Ah... paradise lost.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.950
I think I'm starting to see
the new balance of power in our family.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:04.700
Mom!

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.750
Let me help, I want to learn how to cook.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.910
Okay, then I'll share with you what I know
about making it as yummy as can be.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.950
When you're frying up pork, you should let it
get back to room temperature just beforehand.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.120
You should wait to season it with salt and pepper
until right before you put it on the heat.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.040
Shitake mushrooms shouldn't be washed,
but rather wiped down with a wet cloth.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.410
Wow! You sure keep a lot of different things in mind
when you're cooking, mom!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.040
Well, my biggest goal is for you and Ryo
to grow up nice and healthy

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.330
so all of this is just the natural result
of working towards that.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:28.290
Hm?

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.790
Could it be? Did you meet someone
that you want to cook for?!

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.410
There's a Magical Girl in the neighborhood
who has a problem with maintaining good nutrition.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.120
Wait, a Magical Girl?!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.160
Yeah, I'm worried she'll collapse from malnutrition
long before I have the chance to beat her!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.160
I hope they're ready soon, I can't wait!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.120
Oh, that's right.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.910
There's been a lot going on lately and I ended up
agreeing to help a Magical Girl out for a while.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.910
Is this the same girl that you ran along
the riverbank with the other day?

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:53.870
That's right! I'll share more details with you later.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.160
I always figured this might be the path you'd take, Yuko.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.200
Instead of just beating the Magical Girl,
you'd befriend her in order to release the seal.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.120
Huh? I wouldn't say I've befriended her.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.950
It's more like there was so much pressure,
I had no choice but to agree to help her.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:06.700
It was rough.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:07.620
"Rough"?

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.450
Ah, I think the food might be ready now!

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.950
It looks so yummy! And it smells great, too.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.580
Okay, then let's split it up.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:14.790
Here.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:15.950
Wow! Thanks so much!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:16.500
And for you.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.330
Thanks.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.200
It's delicious! Super yummy!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.660
I'm so glad my hard work paid off!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.660
From now on, I think I can overcome any mountains that
get in my way by just remembering this okonomiyaki!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.250
I'm so glad to hear you're enjoying it.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:32.040
It's got mayonnaise, sauce, and bonito flakes on top!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.500
Not to mention it doesn't have a tofu base,
so I can really taste the wheat flour!

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.700
Though I won't deny I like tofu, too.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.410
That's not exactly a shining endorsement.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.160
I promise I'll try a little harder
to improve your palette from now on!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.450
I'll serve you up some more, Ryo.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.250
Thanks.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.410
No thanks necessary!

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.620
This is all to celebrate your big sister's accomplishment,
so feel free to stuff yourself full!

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.330
Ow, hot!

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.410
Um, Sis? I want to help you out, too.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.410
Huh?

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.000
B-but, Ryo you're still too young.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.120
And I made Momo conceal her identity from you before.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:00.830
Please? I've been reading a lot of books lately
and I think I could be of some use!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.040
My dream is to become your trusted advisor!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.080
I want to watch from your fortress as you charge
into battle atop a horse, leading an army behind you!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.620
I told you before, I don't actually
control an army and don't have plans to!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.620
It's never going to be like this!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.620
Ancestor, are you okay?

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.700
I'll give you some juice and okonomiyaki.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.790
Ugh... is that you, Ryoko?

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.540
Pant. Pant...

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.040
I appreciate you being so kind
to a little ol' doorstop like me.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.620
When my full powers have returned, I promise you
control over North America after I conquer the world!

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:33.500
Huh? Sorry, I think that I'd prefer my sister
to be the one who holds control over all domains.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.120
Will you settle for just being the conqueror in name only?

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:36.950
Huh?! That's driving a hard bargain, don't you think?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.950
Actually, for someone so modest,
you really don't mince words!

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.120
Wobble

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.910
Shamiko, would you mind giving me some ice water?

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.120
Sure thing.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:42.910
Huh?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.950
Mom! Something's wrong with the refrigerator!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.450
It doesn't feel cool!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:47.830
Huh?!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.830
Neither the fridge nor the freezer
sound like they're working.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.660
It is quite old. I wonder if it finally broke down?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.660
That power outage earlier could be part of it.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.910
Is this... fate adjusting to make us pay?

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:04.790
Scrub

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.160
It's fine!

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.580
You know, I've really been wanting
one of those fancy, new fridges.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.200
I'm actually HAPPY that our old one broke on us!

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.790
Mom, have you totally lost it?!

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.870
When that lightning came down earlier,
I heard something go ZAP.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.500
ZAP

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.450
That must have been the refrigerator's dying breath.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:15.500
It'll take a week for a new fridge to be delivered. That's a
problem because right now we're at the start of summer.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.750
We have to figure out how to deal
with all the food I bought to stock up.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.580
We cannot let any of it go to waste!

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.910
I'm going to start cooking all of it right now
and we'll eat it all by tomorrow! Let's speed eat!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.580
Huh?!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:26.290
I'm already full to the point that I wasn't
going to eat breakfast tomorrow!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:30.540
By the way, it took all of our money to buy a new fridge
so make sure you stuff yourselves before we fast!

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.330
That's not how humans work, you know!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.450
Time to get cooking!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.370
What's up? Why did you come in the rain?

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.000
To do reconnaissance on my enemy.
How are you feeling?

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.540
I still have a fever, but I think
I should be back at school by next week.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:46.450
What's that?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:51.330
I came to invade your big, fancy refrigerator
and lay claim to some of it with our Demon delicacies.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.410
Does that mean you're sharing your food?

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.540
That's another way you could put it!

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.540
The bag is filled with a bunch of smaller side dishes.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:58.540
And the big box has pork, bean sprout and egg stew.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:00.040
There's also some chicken hamburg steak in it, too.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:00.870
Wow.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.750
I helped to make some of it myself.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:05.450
If you put them all in the fridge,
they should last for the next two days.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.450
Thank you.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.040
I normally don't get to eat stuff like this,
so I'm really happy.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.000
Gah...

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.370
D-don't get the wrong idea, Magical Girl!

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:17.580
All of this nourishing food is just meant to help you
cultivate more blood so I can steal it later!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.080
And, um...

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.700
I can't think of any other reasons!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.200
Take care of yourself!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.500
Be careful with all the rain!

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.330
Don't give up, Shamiko!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.660
Pick up the fight tomorrow and work to put
more delicious food on your dining table!

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.040
Shamiko.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.200
Momo, you must be over your cold now.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.750
Yeah. Thanks to you.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:46.500
Come with me.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:51.500
Soring through with pink logic

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.830
Bean sprouts and pork sure are yummy, huh?

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.250
I also recommend cabbage and pork together.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.450
Shamiko, raise your arms up.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.450
Huh? What for?

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:56.950
Wha-?

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.000
Okay, let's start your training!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.830
Training?! Huh?! What is all this?!

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:05.000
This is a tire designed for large vehicles
that carry heavy things like in mines and...

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.200
I'm not asking you to explain what type of tire it is!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.290
It won't come off!

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.410
What do you mean by "training"?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.410
I explained it to you before, remember?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.950
I want you to help me keep the city safe.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:18.500
Because you took some of my blood,
the strength of my magic has fallen drastically.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:19.700
Right...

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:22.160
That's why I need you to become stronger.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.410
I understand that.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.870
Which is exactly why I made sure to get a really big tire!

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.500
THAT'S WHERE YOU START TO LOSE ME!

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.540
Hm... how can I best explain it to you?

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.000
Do you understand why I'm strong enough
to stop a dump trunk with only one hand?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.660
Because you have the spirit
and muscle necessary to do so.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.790
That's not it.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.040
The moment that Magical Girls
make a contract with the Light Clan,

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.120
their bodies get pretty much entirely reformatted

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.910
and they become an ether
of incredibly high-density magic.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:49.700
Thus, the reason I can do stuff like this isn't because
of my muscle, but because of the magic within me.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.540
But I thought that you lost a bunch of your magic power?

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.250
Right now, I'm basically making up for that
with my spirit and muscle.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.660
So it's because of your muscles, like I thought.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.700
Even if you're not capable of everything that I am,
you still have your own Demon powers.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.700
You should be able to pull off some similar feats.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:04.330
No...

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:07.000
That's why my goal is to boost your magic.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Magic is part of your body,
your spirit, your life experiences.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.620
There are a lot of ways to train to increase it.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.580
And we're going to start with the easiest,
which is building muscle.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.620
And while you're building muscle,
you can build some muscle.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.160
And top it off with building muscle.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.870
Th-this is scary. I can't get away because of the tire!

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.080
Also, I forgot to mention this,
but we'll also work to build muscle.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:26.660
Forget is the exact opposite of what you did!

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:30.370
If you ask me, I think you just
love training to build muscle!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.250
That's not right. I just can't help it.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.040
Which means you like it!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:38.200
From where I stand you seem as strong as ever,
did you really get weaker?

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.200
Yep.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.620
Also, I can't untie this.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:45.160
My maximum supply of magic power dropped, which
means I can't use any of my most powerful techniques.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:48.330
You have a repertoire of powerful techniques?!
I want to hear all about them!

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.580
Hey, hey! Does this include that
"Fresh Peach Heart Shower" thing you mentioned?!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.870
Why did you commit little details like that to memory?
That's just a mid-level technique.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.410
Which means you can still use it even now, right?!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.700
I want to see it! Get on top of the tire!
Get up there and use that technique!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.660
Do it! Go up there and show me!

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:02.950
I don't want you to see, it's embarrassing.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.000
WHAAAAT?!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.870
Huh? What are you two doing over there?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.250
Oh, it's Anri.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.910
Both Shami-cen's horn and heart seem like they might break in two

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.910
Is "Shamicen" supposed to refer to me?

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:13.370
Wow, so you're going to be working together then.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.660
We're not working together.
We just declared a cease-fire.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:16.370
Indeed.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:19.540
You must be really happy
that you're able to talk freely now, Shamicen.

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.580
But you're looking kind of pale in the face. Are you okay?

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.870
Yes... I'm recovering from a hangover
for reasons I won't go into.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.910
Is "Shamicen" a nickname for her?

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:26.700
It's adorable.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.200
"Shamiko's ascendant" put those together
and you get Shami-cen!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.330
Would it be all right if I called you by that name, too?

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.540
I beg you... can you at least be the one
who shows me some actual respect?

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.160
I see how it is.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.620
You're training muscle so that
you can build up your magic power.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.000
But listen, Momochiyo.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.120
As a rule of thumb, humans don't pull tires
that are designed for mining vehicles.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.040
Nod, nod.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.580
Oh, I see.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.410
That makes sense.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:50.080
I hadn't put any consideration into Shamiko's unique trait
of being unable to carry heavy things.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.790
Right, right. But in this case, that's not unique
to Shamiko and applies to all of humanity.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.700
For now, I think it would be good for her to start with
something that weighs about as much as Shami-cen.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.410
Ancestor!

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.620
Having Shamiko start with this giant tire
is making the hurdle too high.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.700
What if you started her out
with something more lightweight first?

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:04.330
That makes sense.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:08.290
Thank heavens, I'm saved. I can't tell you how happy I am
to have you as a friend, Anri.

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:13.120
Also, hey... when it comes to Shamiko, she's pretty timid
about a lot of things. She's mentally weak and fragile.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.410
Don't you think it would be good to train her
how to be more courageous and gutsier?

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.120
That makes sense!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.080
Like going bungie jumping, or standing under a waterfall.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:18.450
Huh?

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.750
That makes sense. Got anything else?

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.040
Spending the night in an abandoned
and possibly haunted hotel?

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.120
Forget it! Don't listen to any more of Anri's advice!

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:28.580
Later!

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.540
Bye-bye.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:30.500
Thanks.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:31.660
Oh, that's right.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.790
I have a job that might be the perfect fit for you, Shamiko!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.620
I'll give you the details some other time!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:36.410
See ya!

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.200
She had a lot of great ideas
that I never would have thought of.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.410
Good grief. I never know if she's a friend or foe.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.830
Tell me, what is the one thing that you're most afraid of?

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.910
Do you really think I'm going to tell you after all that?

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:52.700
If you want to protect the city, then don't you think
YOU should be working hard to regain your magic?

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:56.330
I promise I'll do my best,
so you tell me what YOU'RE most afraid of.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.700
I took your magic so I don't have a choice,
but we're still in this together.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.040
"In it together"? I hadn't thought about it like that.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.160
I see. You have a point.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:08.040
Something I'm afraid of... something scary...

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:10.660
I'm scared of stuffed mochi balls.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.000
What...?

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.040
I'm not talking about the plain ones, either.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.750
There's a particular shop in the Tama Sakura
shopping district that sells these.

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.450
They're strawberry stuffed mochi balls.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.580
The strawberry is abnormally large and the mochi skin
is super thin so you can see the red paste inside

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.160
which gives it a really unsettling appearance.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.160
Size Comparison

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:27.160
Plus it's even got a rich cream inside
that makes it the absolute peak of decadence.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.290
I haven't eaten one for years.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.160
Here, take my purse.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.500
Okay, let's start by conquering that!

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.790
Quiver in fear, Magical Girl!

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:37.120
Heh, heh, heh, triple heh.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:40.580
Their evening stock
usually sells out really fast, so run for it!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:41.830
Roger!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.870
If you can manage it, try and buy two!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:49.200
Just take a look! The thin mochi
covering the dark red bean paste!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.750
I ran really fast and had to wait in line,
but I managed to get two!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.410
Now, quiver in fear! Embrace the absolute terror!
Come on, come on!

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.160
Are you shaking in your boots yet, Magical Girl?

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.750
Ha, ha, ha!

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.700
HA
HA
HA

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.410
HA
HA
HA

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.290
Ha, ha... Huh?

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:05.790
Momo?

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.950
Here. One of them is for you, Shamiko.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:08.790
Huh?

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.370
Huh?

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:14.080
You ran really far and fast to go and get them, right?

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.160
Having a bit of a sugary snack
after a workout is extra delicious.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:19.910
Nice running out there. These mochi balls
are the tastiest when you eat them fresh.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.200
You tricked me into all this, didn't you?!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.620
Dizzy-wizzy...

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.330
Sh-she pulled one over on me.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.790
Don't think this means you've...

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:30.410
JUMP

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.160
It's super yummy!

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.580
Yum, yum.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:36.080
I didn't lie about not being able
to handle these mochi balls.

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:37.330
Huh?

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:41.200
Because they make me remember the past.
That's why I've avoided eating them for years.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.580
My sister used to love the sweets from that shop.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:48.700
Do you... have a sister?

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:51.580
Yeah. We're not blood-related though.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.370
I don't have any family...

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:57.830
Since you're doing your best to train,
I've decided to face the things I'm bad at.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.540
I'll learn to embrace my past and everything in it.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:03.540
It might help me get my magic back to normal, too.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:05.910
I'll take a seat and eat.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.120
Uh, fer sure!

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:10.790
Gah, she caught me off guard
so my reply came out all weird.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.290
I'm just gonna eat the darn thing!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.080
Shamiko.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:13.790
Huh?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.200
I'm sorry for forcing you to help me out.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.830
Why apologize all of a sudden?

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:18.660
Chew

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.290
Chew

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:19.910
Chew

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:20.540
Chew

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.160
Chew

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.450
If you feel bad about it,

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.040
then you should tell me something
you're actually scared of next time.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:28.790
Chew

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.830
All right.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.120
Then...

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:35.750
I'm scared of drinking cold tea
together with you, Shamiko.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:36.870
Roger that!

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.910
But you're not going to trick me a third time!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.290
That was fast.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:44.830
You owe me a dollar!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.700
Please Shamiko... offer me some cold tea, too...

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.540
So, are we about wrapped up for today?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:56.580
Huh? I'd say we're just getting started, don't you?

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:57.080
Huh?

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.120
Do you have a curfew, Shamiko?

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.580
Let's start with some stretches and squats.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.950
I thought we were putting the muscle building on hold...

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:09.370
It's totally ineffective if you only train your mental muscles
without training your muscle muscles.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:09.370
Muscle muscles?

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.200
There are a wide variety of methods to build muscle
without having to carry anything heavy, you know!

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.580
Momo, you're terrifying me!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.370
Twenty-six.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:17.830
Twenty-six

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.540
Twenty-seven.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:20.120
Twenty-seven

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.410
I'll let you go home once you're able to move the tire.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.790
Twenty-eight.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:30.620
Twenty-nine... Twenty-nine point five...

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:31.660
Don't give up, Shamiko! Train both your body and mind
to overcome all the things that scare you!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.290
Why aren't you going up to thirty?!

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.160
Sunday Morn

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.120
Yo, Shamiko!

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.410
About that job I mentioned to you before,
can you make it today?

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:38.620
Another job, huh?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.370
EVENT: Meet & Greet
with Miss Tama Sakura

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.330
This is such a huge help!

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.580
Shamiko! Hey girl! Long time, no see!

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.870
The person who was originally supposed to do it
suddenly strained their back, so we were in trouble.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.620
Come and sell wieners again sometime.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:50.540
I don't know if I'm really cut out to handle such
an important role as the person inside the mascot...

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.700
You're the only one we can count on, Shamiko!

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:53.830
R-really?

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.620
Really! We need someone lit-

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:58.370
I mean someone with a compact form
chosen by God for this important duty!

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:00.580
You were looking for someone little, I get it.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:11.580
Miss Tama Sakura

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:03.450
A fairy born from within an ancient cherry blossom tree.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.910
A fairy born from within an ancient cherry blossom tree

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.410
Specialty: Backflipping Piping Hot Oden Soup.

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.950
Specialty: Backflipping Piping Hot Oden Soup

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.660
It can produce an unlimited supply
of highly-addictive candy from its oversized teacup

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:10.290
It can produce an unlimited supply of highly-addictive candy
from its oversized teacup to brainwash children

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.250
and use it to brainwash children.

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:11.870
"Highly-addictive candy"?!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.290
Even if you don't move around much,
it's a pretty labor-intensive job.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:19.000
Come to the changing room every 20 or 30 minutes
to take a break and drink water.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.870
Ugh, this thing is pretty heavy and really hot.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.040
I wanna see the backflip!

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:25.200
Give us some of that super tasty candy!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.580
Is it true that you're really good at using nunchucks?

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:27.580
This mascot is pretty well-known in town!

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.330
Do that move where you climb the wall
with a ninja dagger!

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.620
Candy... please, the candy!

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.200
They really laid it on thick with the character quirks!

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:34.950
Aren't you going to do the backflip
into the piping hot oden soup?!

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.830
Is that really something
Miss Tama Sakura normally does?!

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.830
Candy! Use your ninja dagger! Candy! Give us the candy!

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:41.330
I-I'll admit it's a little fun to be this popular with little kids,

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.700
but just passing out the fliers and candy
is causing more than enough chaos!

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:45.410
Be careful!

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:47.540
Are you all right?

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:49.580
You really surprised me
by nearly falling back into the fountain like that.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:50.500
Huh? Whose voice is that?

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:51.870
I can't see anything!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:53.950
Come now children, can't you see
the nice kitty is having trouble?

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.410
Be good and make an orderly line.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.290
Who is that?

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.910
Are you okay? Your head is a little off center.

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:00.370
I'll help you out, so let's get it back to normal.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:01.580
Thank you very much.

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:09.500
If they pick up on it, some really weird people
might start coming around here.

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:14.500
In the worst-case scenario, you, your family and all
the Demons that live here might end up being hunted.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.250
Can you see properly now?

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:16.830
Yeah.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.410
I can see some clothes indicative of someone
I really don't want to see!

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:33.950
The Demon Girl Next Door

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:41.200
Sassouto shobu shite

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:42.750
Yatchau kedo makechatte

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:43.950
Fugainai nai ne

00:22:43.950 --> 00:22:45.500
Shoushin tenshin

00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:46.910
Kibun wa sunsun demo

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:48.580
Shippo de henji shiyou

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:52.370
Chounai de waiwai shite

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:53.950
Inu made bow-wow de

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:55.250
Tende meimei de

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:56.700
Shunka shuutou

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:00.000
Shippai shita tte waraitobasou

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:06.500
Ano koro to onaji you ni kokoro tsumuide

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:12.330
Kono machi de deaeta kiseki

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.080
Kanaete yo

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:21.870
Zenkai da wa tire shou ippai

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:24.660
Warning mada kikikanri enjoy

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:30.200
Toridori saita iro canvas kakenuke

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.080
Sunset da wa, kangaete bakari ja

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:35.330
Sou, mae!

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:40.080
Hora, donna iro datte yume kasanete

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:41.870
Motto asobou ne

00:23:50.950 --> 00:24:06.000
Preview

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:54.500
Wha-wha-what? Now there's Magical Girls
starting to pop up everywhere!

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.250
It's okay, I called her here.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:57.830
I don't know what you mean by things being "okay"?!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:24:00.660
Hold on a second, I think I should
introduce myself properly first.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.790
Don't bother, the viewers will get all they need to know
in the next episode.

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:06.000
The Cursed fruit!! Beware the Sour Mikan!!

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:03.580
Huh?

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:04.700
You really surprised me

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:06.000
by showing up already transformed!
